he new compass design for everybody to test. The new compass is highly configurable in the menu (\"Compass Style\" - this menu is accessible during ...\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    22 Jun 2026, 12:57\n    Forum: OSTC+, 3, cR, sport, nano and OSTC 2 (Mod. 2015 and later)\n    Topic: Firmware update 10.97 Problem beim OSTC Sport\n    Replies: 8\n    Views: 33374\n\n### Re: Firmware update 10.97 Problem beim OSTC Sport\n\nHallo,\nDie Firmware 10.97 läuft erst, wenn sie installiert wurde. Die hat zumindest mal mit dem Updateproblem hier absolut nichts zu tun. Schicke den OSTC im Zweifelsfall zu uns, wir bekommen das schon installiert.\nGruß,\nMatthias\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    15 Jun 2026, 15:48\n    Forum: OSTC+, 3, cR, sport, nano and OSTC 2 (Mod. 2015 and later)\n    Topic: Firmware update 10.97 Problem beim OSTC Sport\n    Replies: 8\n    Views: 33374\n\n### Re: Firmware update 10.97 Problem beim OSTC Sport\n\nBei \"OSTConf\" (Der iPhone App, die Du vermutlich meinst) geht nur BLE. Hier mal im OSTC reset menü ein \"Reset-Bluetooth\" auswählen.\nGruß,\nMatthias\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    12 Jun 2026, 19:00\n    Forum: OSTC Mk.2, 2N and 2C (Sold between 2007 and 2014)\n    Topic: OSTC Mk2 Screen staying dark\n    Replies: 4\n    Views: 47739\n\n### Re: OSTC Mk2 Screen staying dark\n\nI agree, this looks like the unit is end-of-life unfortunately.\nMatthias\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    11 Jun 2026, 11:09\n    Forum: OSTC+, 3, cR, sport, nano and OSTC 2 (Mod. 2015 and later)\n    Topic: Firmware update 10.97 Problem beim OSTC Sport\n    Replies: 8\n    Views: 33374\n\n### Re: hwOS TECH: New Firmware 3.33\n\nfixed in the 3.34...\n[3.34]\nBUGFIX: Compass showed 000 when dive mode was started out of sleep mode\nNEW: Support for new hardware versions (OSTC+ only)\nBUGFIX: String \"Höhle\" was not properly shown (German version only)\nBUGFIX: Digital S8 Interface could delay startup on OSTC+ S8 in rare caes\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    27 Mar 2026, 09:16\n    Forum: OSTC+, 3, cR, sport, nano and OSTC 2 (Mod. 2015 and later)\n    Topic: comparison 2, nano or +?\n    Replies: 3\n    Views: 46511\n\n### Re: comparison 2, nano or +?\n\nThe battery compartment in the OSTC+ and the USB port in the OSTC nano are watertight. This is fine for a small leak or in freshwater, but if you dive a week-long liveaboard with a leaking battery cap or missing USB cap, both units will suffer damage.\nRegards,\nMatthias\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    23 Mar 2026, 20:51\n    Forum: OSTC 4 and OSTC 5\n    Topic: hwOS4: New Firmware 1.7.5 with RTE 3.70\n    Replies: 10\n    Views: 83130\n\n### Re: hwOS4: New Firmware 1.7.5 with RTE 3.70\n\nYes, in bailout mode the OSTC 4 usues normal OC calculations for decompression and ppO2 warnings.\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    22 Mar 2026, 17:34\n    Forum: OSTC+, 3, cR, sport, nano and OSTC 2 (Mod. 2015 and later)\n    Topic: comparison 2, nano or +?\n    Replies: 3\n    Views: 46511\n\n### Re: comparison 2, nano or +?\n\nHi,\nI have our comparison sheet attached here. If you don't mind the slightly smaller display, the OSTC nano is very popular right now. Especially for CCR divers (as a backup with fixed setpoints).\nRegards,\nMatthias\n\n  * Jump to post\n\nby heinrichsweikamp\n    25 Feb 2026, 16:06\n    Forum: OSTC+, 3, cR, sport, nano and OSTC 2 (Mod. 2015 and later)\n    Topic: hwOS TECH: New Firmware 3.33\n    Replies: 29\n    Views: 303113\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOSTC 4 and OSTC 5 - Page 2 - forum.heinrichsweikamp.com (https://www.forum.heinrichsweikamp.com/viewforum.php?f=7&sid=b7fe7dcb25c00ab0f3d9ef0006e98d16&start=25)\nciteturn9search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n# forum.heinrichsweikamp.com\n\nheinrichs weikamp user & developer forum\n\n## OSTC 4 and OSTC 5\n\nOSTC running hwOS4 Firmware\n\n236 topics\n